ssor MLB manifest design;\n[L27] - canonical `ecq-synthesis-v1` registration;\n[L28] - multiple architecture gates around synthesis;\n[L29] - a new FixedDec value contract;\n[L30] - exhaustive cross-seat certification of every later layer.\n\n[L32] Those entered later.\n\n---\n\n[L36] # B. EXPECTED SIZE OF WORK\n\n[L38] ### Classification: **NORMAL BUILD**\n\n[L40] It was larger than bounded maintenance because there was no current React web surface on disk and a new vertical slice had to be assembled.\n\n[L42] It was **not initially an architecture-change request** because Gate 6 architecture and Parent Quant methodology already existed and the intended first pass explicitly fit inside them.\n\n[L44] A sane estimate of the original work shape was:\n\n[L46] **inspect existing repo → build adapter/contracts/API projection → React view → tests → show Don.**\n\n[L48] The first slice legitimately required engineering discipline, but it did **not** require repeated governance expansion.\n\n---\n\n[L52] # C. ACTUAL WORK PERFORMED\n\n[L54] Only concrete built/tested outcomes are counted here.\n\n[L56] ### 1. React DevPad / Baseline slice — genuinely built\n\n[L58] A Vite/React/TypeScript DevPad was created over the frozen MLB fixture.\n\n[L60] It materially provided:\n\n[L62] - 12-game MLB PREGAME slate;\n[L63] - event selection;\n[L64] - separate BASELINE view;\n[L65] - component/evidence drill-down;\n[L66] - provenance;\n[L67] - uncertainty/evidence state;\n[L68] - generic sport-module boundary;\n[L69] - immutable Baseline;\n[L70] - deterministic state identity;\n[L71] - injected clock;\n[L72] - read-only enforcement.\n\n[L74] This was a **real visible product outcome**.\n\n[L76] ### 2. SHA-256 defect — genuinely found and fixed\n\n[L78] Initial implementation contained a broken custom SHA-256 padding calculation.\n\n[L80] Luce correctly found that hashes labeled SHA-256 did not match standards.\n\n[L82] Nico/Big Pickle then actually repaired:\n\n[L84] - SHA-256 padding;\n[L85] - fixed-vector tests;\n[L86] - Node crypto cross-checks;\n[L87] - derived state identity;\n[L88] - browser compatibility;\n[L89] - app→test dependency.\n\n[L91] Result reached:\n\n[L93] **37/37 tests + clean build.**\n\n[L95] This was valid corrective work.\n\n[L97] ### 3. Don Delta — genuinely built\n\n[L99] A second independently addressable view was implemented:\n\n[L101] **Human input → classification → validation → Don Delta.**\n\n[L103] Actual implementation included:\n\n[L105] - immutable human input records;\n[L106] - classification surface;\n[L107] - validation state;\n[L108] - append-only Don Delta ledger;\n[L109] - supersession;\n[L110] - write authority;\n[L111] - anti-lookahead;\n[L112] - deterministic replay;\n[L113] - React Don Delta UI;\n[L114] - three-view routing.\n\n[L116] Result eventually reached:\n\n[L118] **73/73 tests.**\n\n[L120] ### 4. Clock/vocabulary repair — genuinely implemented\n\n[L122] The Don Delta implementation was revised so that:\n\n[L124] - `RunClock` pinned a declared run instant;\n[L125] - authoritative writes stopped depending on accidental execution-time variance;\n[L126] - validation became:\n[L127]   `UNVALIDATED / VALIDATED / REFUTED / EXPIRED`;\n[L128] - verification became the orthogonal:\n[L129]   `FULL / PARTIAL / UNVERIFIABLE`;\n[L130] - Don Delta envelope was versioned appropriately.\n\n[L132] Result reached:\n\n[L134] **94/94 tests.**\n\n[L136] ### 5. Generic Model Synthesis shell — genuinely built\n\n[L138] The third state was materially implemented as generic infrastructure:\n\n[L140] - Model Synthesis envelope;\n[L141] - deterministic identity;\n[L142] - exact Baseline lineage;\n[L143] - exact Don Delta lineage;\n[L144] - append-only synthesis history;\n[L145] - write authority;\n[L146] - replay;\n[L147] - anti-lookahead;\n[L148] - React Model Synthesis view;\n[L149] - NON-CANON transcript transform;\n[L150] - loud failure when the canonical MLB transform did not exist.\n\n[L152] This was another **real