 onset is when the session moved from:\n\n[L225] > **“Model Synthesis shell exists and correctly fails loudly because canonical MLB synthesis semantics are absent.”**\n\nto:\n\n[L229] > **“Now let's make canonical `ecq-synthesis-v1@1.0.0` executable inside this same DevPad session.”**\n\n[L231] That decision converted a successful product-build session into a methodology + architecture + contract-reconciliation program.\n\n[L233] At that point the shell itself had already proven the boundary correctly: **SPORT GAP → Corrado**.\n\n[L235] Instead of closing the DevPad build at that visible checkpoint, the session continued into:\n\n[L237] Corrado semantics → Nico math core → Luce → lane correction → Corrado → Nico → Luce → Chiave → Corrado value materialization → Chiave new contract freeze.\n\n[L239] That is the clearest loop branch.\n\n---\n\n[L243] # E. LOOP MECHANISM\n\n[L245] The loop became:\n\n[L247] **Don → Coda framing → Nico → Luce → Coda → next layer → Nico → Luce → Coda → specialty seat → Nico → Luce → architecture gate → new contract → next implementation.**\n\n[L249] More specifically:\n\n[L251] ### Phase 1 — Healthy\n\n[L253] **Coda → Nico → Luce**\n\n[L255] Baseline React slice.\n\n[L257] Luce found a real SHA problem.\n\n[L259] **Nico fix → Luce reverify.**\n\n[L261] This was normal build/verify/fix.\n\n[L263] ### Phase 2 — Still productive, but expanding\n\n[L265] **Don authorizes Don Delta → Nico → Luce.**\n\n[L267] Luce finds clock/vocabulary issues.\n\n[L269] Instead of treating this as one bounded closure patch, orchestration added:\n\n[L271] - pre-Slice-3 reconciliation;\n[L272] - special Nico grounding;\n[L273] - Coda reconciliation;\n[L274] - separate repair verification;\n[L275] - final Coda reconciliation.\n\n[L277] Useful work occurred, but process started expanding around the work.\n\n[L279] ### Phase 3 — Generic Model Synthesis\n\n[L281] **Don → Nico → Luce.**\n\n[L283] Again productive. A visible third view existed.\n\n[L285] But then the