ted reconciliation layer.\n[L357] - validation vocabulary → contract migration.\n[L358] - lane-map mismatch → specialty-seat reroute.\n[L359] - shell references-only evidence → architecture gate.\n\n[L361] The problem was not Luce finding them; the problem was orchestration repeatedly turning findings into **new lifecycle stages**.\n\n[L363] ### Coda inferred or extended architecture\n\n[L365] The largest example was proposing a separate `SynthesisOverlayValueSet` / value-materialization layer before Chiave's formal freeze.\n\n[L367] That idea turned out to be sensible, but it was nevertheless a **new architectural object introduced while the original DevPad session was still open**.\n\n[L369] ### Builder interruption\n\n[L371] Dots3 was interrupted and replaced by Big Pickle due to repeated stalls.\n\n[L373] Later Nico's work was repeatedly stopped at semantic seams and handed to:\n\n[L375] Corrado → Luce → Chiave → Corrado → Chiave.\n\n[L377] Those later interruptions were often justified by authority boundaries, but they prevented a single coherent \"build → show → close\" rhythm.\n\n[L379] ### Same question effectively answered repeatedly\n\n[L381] Examples:\n\n[L383] - \"Is Slice 1 done?\" answered by builder, then Luce, then Coda.\n[L384] - \"Is Slice 2 ready?\" builder → Luce → pre-Slice-3 repair → Luce → Coda.\n[L385] - \"Is Model Synthesis ready?\" shell implementation → Luce → Corrado → math implementation → Luce → lane fix → Luce → Chiave.\n[L386] - \"Can canonical synthesis execute?\" repeatedly approached from shell, methodology, math core, lane maps, then value surface.\n\n[L388] ### Confidence decreased despite more work\n\n[L390] A major example:\n\n[L392] Generic Model Synthesis shell was green and honest.\n\n[L394] Then pursuing canonical execution exposed that the state model did **not actually contain executable human delta magnitudes**.\n\n[L396] So after more work, the system knew more—but the path to canonical registration became **less complete than initially assumed**.\n\n[L398] That is a classic sign of scope outrunning ground truth.\n\n[L400] ### Certification replaced visible progress\n\n[L402] The period after the Model Synthesis shell became visible produced many:\n\n[L404] - handoffs;\n[L405] - test counts;\n[L406] - rulings;\n[L407] - gate verdicts;\n[L408] - semantic definitions;\n[L409] - re-verifications;\n\n[L411] but **no corresponding new end-user capability appeared in the React DevPad**.\n\n---\n\n[L415] # F. ASSUMPTIONS / INVENTED STATE\n\n[L417] | ClaimClassificationFinding                                             |                                            |                                                                         |\n[L418] | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------ | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n[L419] | Frozen MLB data could drive a React Baseline surface                   | **VERIFIED**                               | It did.                                                                 |\n[L420] | Baseline could be deterministic/read-only                              | **VERIFIED**                               | Tests and Luce established it.                                          |\n[L421] | Original SHA implementation was standards-compliant                    | **ASSUMED → FALSE**                        | Luce disproved it.                                                      |\n[L422] | Don Delta could be implemented separately from Baseline                | **VERIFIED**                               | Built and tested.                                                       |\n[L423] | `SystemClock()` wiring was replay-safe                                 | **ASSUMED → INCOMPLETE**                   | Needed pinned RunClock.                                                 |\n[L424] | Slice-2 five-state validation vocabulary matched Par