y.\\r\\n Coda = strategic advisor / governance.\\r\\n Corrado = technical stack methodology / design-build seat, model-agnostic.\\r\\n Chiave = architecture gate only when material.\\r\\n Ragno = Principal Consultant / integration / translation.\\r\\n Calibro = implementation design, model-agnostic.\\r\\n Talon = operations/routing.\\r\\n Keel = build/test/evidence.\\r\\n Luce = verification / ground truth.\\r\\n IDENTITY != ROLE != LENS != PERSONALITY != AUTHORITY != MODEL.\\r\\n MODEL != SEAT.\\r\\n Proceed / Checkpoint / Stop / Escalate protocol remains active.\\r\\nOperating Lessons to Preserve\\r\\n Cleanup first, then operate; let real regressions expose what needs surgical hardening.\\r\\n Do not switch model/runtime mid-flight during heavy stateful execution unless intentionally testing \\r\\nsubstitution.\\r\\n Big Pickle remains a strong default candidate for upper-tier heavy stateful operational work with seat￾specific bootstraps.\\r\\n Use Kimi/Corrado early as a high-inference methodology challenger, then remove it from the active loop \\r\\nonce the needed synthesis is harvested.\\r\\n Shared-state architecture remains end-state-first: heterogeneous operator interfaces and compute nodes \\r\\naround one synchronized live state engine; capability inventory is distinct from live state; prepared state\\r\\nis distinct from committed state.\\r\\nWhat This Chat Added to Framework Thinking\\r\\n A stronger proof of MODEL != SEAT through direct model auditions and cognitive-role mapping.\\r\\n Provider/runtime reliability should be treated as a first-class operating variable, separate from cognitive \\r\\nsuitability.\\r\\n Distributed challenge and verification are preferable to one final gatekeeper in analytical systems.\\r\\n Do not over-engineer future architecture before real failures prove the need.GCE Framework Handoff — 2026-09-18\\r\\nImmediate Framework Re-entry\\r\\n1. Keep Edge Crew work out of the main framework chat except when it creates a reusable framework \\r\\nlesson.\\r\\n2. Resume the active GCE build/state from its latest accepted handoff rather than redesigning it from EC \\r\\nconcepts.\\r\\n3. Revisit the command-center / identity-runtime split, shared-state engine, and direct runtime method \\r\\nonly as current framework priorities require.\\r\\n4. Preserve provenance and latest accepted state; no broad redesign.\\r\\nHandoff Question for the Framework Chat\\r\\nWhat is the latest accepted GCE framework state, what is the next real operational blocker, and what should \\r\\nDon/Coda work on next without importing unnecessary Edge Crew architecture?\"}],\"ref_id\":\"turn6file1\"},{\"version_id\":\"1\",\"name\":\"Pasted text(20260923-211422).txt\",\"mime_type\":\"text/plain\",\"size_bytes\":35453,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-23T21:14:21+00:00\",\"modified_at\":\"2026-09-23T21:14:21.887478+00:00\",\"file_provider\":\"native\",\"library_file_id\":\"libfile_cfe0d6e23f2c8191a5f0e887983e33ee\",\"role\":\"editor\",\"result_index\":2,\"file_id\":\"file_00000000518481fd98108149cb33a94f\",\"surface\":\"library\",\"score\":0.9915720883092318,\"snippets\":[{\"text\":\"project truth remains elsewhere.  \\r\\n**Status:** SUPPORTING / historical transition package.\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n## Framework local handoff\\r\\n\\r\\n**Artifact:** `GCE_FRAMEWORK_HANDOFF_NEW_CHAT_2026-09-20.docx`  \\r\\n**Type:** handoff  \\r\\n**Location:** `/mnt/data/GCE_FRAMEWORK_HANDOFF_NEW_CHAT_2026-09-20.docx`  \\r\\n**Owner:** Coda / Strategic Governance  \\r\\n**Status:** SUPPORTING, but seat-map details require reconciliation against later 2026-09-22 roster doctrine.\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n## Google Drive — framework research folders created\\r\\n\\r\\nKnown hierarchy:\\r\\n\\r\\n`GCE / GCE_ORG / 01_Executive_Council / 02_Technical_Strategy_Systems_Intelligence /`\\r\\n\\r\\nCreated folders:\\r\\n\\r\\n- `01_Model_Labor_Intelligence`\\r\\n- `02_Runtime_Provider_Intelligence`\\r\\n- `03_Proving_Grounds`\\r