nce workspace + nested Keel heritage tree; UNKNOWN classification, HOLD.\\n- C:\\\\Users\\\\Dekan AI Brother\\\\GCE_IDENTITY\\\\Talon\\\\ACTION_ITEMS.md: references migration workspace (GX-P0 COMPLETE).\\n- C:\\\\Users\\\\Dekan AI Brother\\\\Desktop\\\\GCE_DON\\\\99_ARCHIVE\\\\GCE_LegacyArchives_2026-09-05\\\\: P5 archive incl. stale twin + O-OPS-2 test battery (provenance only).\\n▣  Compaction · Big Pickle · 33.2s\\n+ Thought: 4.3s\\nThe audit is complete and the report was delivered. Per the hard stop (read-only, no changes), the next step is awaiting Don/Coda decisions — so I'll pause rather than act.\\nHow should I proceed?\\n- Deliver the findings to Don (draft a decision memo with the cleanup candidates + holds)\\n- Deep-verify one of the holds (e.g. GCE_EC8 residency, migration P7, voice-bridge deps)\\n- Begin authorized cleanup once you sign off on the candidate list\\n- Something else\"}],\"ref_id\":\"turn6file4\"},{\"version_id\":\"1\",\"name\":\"Pasted text(3).txt\",\"mime_type\":\"text/plain\",\"size_bytes\":53606,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-24T14:41:45+00:00\",\"modified_at\":\"2026-09-24T14:41:47.811482+00:00\",\"file_provider\":\"native\",\"library_file_id\":\"libfile_697ff1d8ddf48191907a5f24d7667bde\",\"role\":\"editor\",\"result_index\":5,\"file_id\":\"file_00000000525c8246afa617bb83e7e24c\",\"surface\":\"library\",\"score\":0.9841938675629466,\"snippets\":[{\"text\":\"This is an operational exchange lane.\\r\\n\\r\\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\r\\n9. HANDOFF ENVELOPE\\r\\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\r\\n\\r\\nEvery transported handoff should use a structured envelope.\\r\\n\\r\\nWorking schema:\\r\\n\\r\\nHANDOFF_ID:\\r\\nFROM_SEAT:\\r\\nTO_SEAT:\\r\\nPROJECT:\\r\\nWORKSTREAM:\\r\\nTYPE:\\r\\nPRIORITY:\\r\\nSTATUS:\\r\\nCREATED_AT:\\r\\nRETURN_TO:\\r\\n\\r\\nOBJECTIVE:\\r\\n...\\r\\n\\r\\nCONTEXT:\\r\\n...\\r\\n\\r\\nINSTRUCTIONS:\\r\\n...\\r\\n\\r\\nARTIFACTS:\\r\\n...\\r\\n\\r\\nSTOP_CONDITIONS:\\r\\n...\\r\\n\\r\\nEXPECTED_RETURN:\\r\\n...\\r\\n\\r\\nExample:\\r\\n\\r\\nHANDOFF_ID: HDO-20260924-0017\\r\\nFROM_SEAT: Coda\\r\\nTO_SEAT: Luce\\r\\nPROJECT: GCE_DevPad_Command_Center\\r\\nWORKSTREAM: myDon Phase 1\\r\\nTYPE: VERIFICATION\\r\\nPRIORITY: NORMAL\\r\\nSTATUS: READY_TO_TRANSPORT\\r\\n\\r\\nOBJECTIVE:\\r\\nVerify route idempotency and restart persistence.\\r\\n\\r\\nCONTEXT:\\r\\n...\\r\\n\\r\\nRETURN_TO:\\r\\nCoda / Don\\r\\n\\r\\nThe filename should preserve the canonical handoff ID.\\r\\n\\r\\nExample:\\r\\n\\r\\nHDO-20260924-0017_luce_mydon_phase1.md\\r\\n\\r\\nor structured JSON where appropriate.\\r\\n\\r\\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\r\\n10. TWO-WAY REQUIREMENT\\r\\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\r\\n\\r\\nThe Cable Car cannot be outbound-only.\\r\\n\\r\\nCoda sends work into GCE.\\r\\n\\r\\nGCE must return:\\r\\n\\r\\n- findings;\\r\\n- implementation results;\\r\\n- verification;\\r\\n- blockers;\\r\\n- status;\\r\\n- artifacts;\\r\\n- escalation requests.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe same HANDOFF_ID should survive the full round trip.\\r\\n\\r\\nExample:\\r\\n\\r\\nHDO-20260924-0017\\r\\n    outbound Coda → Luce\\r\\n    return Luce → Coda\\r\\n\\r\\nDo not mint a disconnected identity for each leg unless there is a proven need.\\r\\n\\r\\nParent/child IDs may later be added for branching work.\\r\\n\\r\\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\r\\n11. GOOGLE DRIVE MCP ROLE\\r\\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\r\\n\\r\\nThe Drive integration should be evaluated for bounded operations such as:\\r\\n\\r\\n- create handoff artifact;\\r\\n- read handoff artifact;\\r\\n- move to a status folder;\\r\\n- archive completed work;\\r\\n- create return artifact;\\r\\n- inspect transport folder;\\r\\n- reconcile failed/incomplete delivery.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe design should avoid requiring Don to manually:\\r\\n\\r\\n- create files;\\r\\n- rename files;\\r\\n- move files;\\r\\n- copy payloads between folders;\\r\\n- clean up routine transport residue.\\r\\n\\r\\nAutomation should do routine transport housekeeping.\\r\\n\\r\\nDon should intervene only for:\\r\\n\\r\\n- routing authority;\\r\\n- conflict;\\r\\n- ambiguity;\\r\\n- escalation;\\r\\n- destructive cleanup if governance requires approval.\\r\\n\\r\\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\r\\n12. DRIVE CLEANUP / ARCHIVE POLICY\\r\\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\r\\n\\r\\nDon explicitly raised concern about Drive clutter.\\r\\n\\r\\nTherefore cleanup cannot be an afterthought.\\r\\n\\r\\nPotential lifecycle:\\r\\n\\r\\nREADY\\r\\n→ TRANSPORTED\\r\\n→ ACKNOWLEDGED\\r\\n→ COMPLETED\\r\\n→ ARCHIVED\\r\\n\\r\\nTransport artifacts should not remain forever in working folders.\\r\\n\\r\\nCandidate policy:\\r\\n\\r\\n- active/in-flight handoffs remain hot;\\r\\n- completed items move automatically to archive;\\r\\n- older operational transport residue can be compacted;\\r\\n- only artifacts with durable value get promoted into project/framework areas;\\r\\n- Raven/Magpie may later help classify durable records;\\r\\n- cleanup automation should never erase canonical project records.\\r\\n\\r\\nTransport archive != project canon.\\r\\n\\r\\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\r\\n13. RELATIONSHIP TO MAIN / ROOKIE DEVPAD\\r\\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\r\\n\\r\\nCable Car should eventually be able to target either operating surface.\\r\\n\\r\\nMain DevPad:\\r\\n\\r\\n- project-bound;\\r\\n- stable seats;\\r\\n- durable active work.\\r\\n\\r\\nRookie DevPad:\\r\\n\\r\\n- ad hoc;\\r\\n- experimental;\\r\\n- temporary runtime work.\"}],\"source_gizmo_id\":\"g-p-6ab41b7c2620819187c626358eeb8a48\",\"ref_id\":\"turn6file5\"},{\"version_id\":\"1\",\"name\":\"GCE_FRAMEWORK_HANDOFF_v2_GROUNDED_2026-09-18.docx\",\"mime_type\":\"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document\",\"size_bytes\":38615,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-18T17:59:35.692367+00:00\",\"modified_at\":\"2026-09-18T17:59:35.692481+00:00\",\"file_provider\":\"native\",\"library_file_id\":\"libfile_bfaada83bd7c8191acec52e762b2af98\",\"library_artifact_type\":\"report\",\"role\":\"editor\",\"result_index\":6,\"file_id\":\"file_00000000ef0481fdb6bd4081ee79a236\",\"surface\":\"library\",\"score\":0.9803239907042285,\"snippets\":[{\"text\":\"GCE Framework Handoff V2 — 2026-09-18\\r\\nGCE FRAMEWORK HANDOFF V2\\r\\nReturn from Edge Crew tangent to the main GCE stack\\r\\nGrounded reset: 2026-09-18 | Framework reset\\r\\nEdge Crew produced reusable lessons, but it is not the GCE framework itself. Resume framework work \\r\\nfrom the latest accepted GCE handoff and import only durable lessons that genuinely generalize.\\r\\nFramework State to Preserve\\r\\n Don = final authority.\\r\\n Coda = strategic advisor / governance.\\r\\n Corrado = technical stack methodology / design-build seat, model-agnostic.\\r\\n Chiave = architecture gate when material.\\r\\n Ragno = Principal Consultant / integration / translation.\\r\\n Calibro = implementation design, model-agnostic.\\r\\n Talon = operations / routing.\\r\\n Keel = build / test / evidence.\\r\\n Luce = verification / ground truth.\\r\\n IDENTITY != ROLE != LENS != PERSONALITY != AUTHORITY != MODEL.\\r\\n MODEL != SEAT.\\r\\nDurable Lessons Earned From Edge Crew\\r\\n Stage-match the model to the work: POC discovery is not architecture.\\r\\n Do not let an architect model decide what an unfinished POC means before Don/Coda declare the POC \\r\\nready for architecture.\\r\\n Provider/runtime reliability is separate from cognitive suitability.\\r\\n Distributed challenge/verification can be safer than one central gatekeeper.\\r\\n Independence must be demonstrated through provenance and behavior, not assumed from different \\r\\nmodel names.\\r\\n Do not harden architecture faster than operating evidence earns it.\\r\\n One architectural responsibility at a time.\\r\\nWhat This Chat Did NOT Rework\\r\\nThis Edge Crew tangent did not replace the accepted GCE shared-state/end-state architecture, command￾center work, runtime identity split, or current operating priorities. Those should be reloaded from the latest \\r\\ndedicated framework artifacts rather than reconstructed here.\\r\\nFramework Re-entry Rule\\r\\nReturn to the latest accepted framework state, identify the next real operational blocker, and solve that one \\r\\njob. Do not import betting-domain components merely because they were useful in Edge Crew.\"}],\"ref_id\":\"turn6file6\"},{\"version_id\":\"1\",\"name\":\"20260914-TALON-G3-endstate-DECISION-REQUEST.md\",\"mime_type\":\"text/markdown\",\"size_bytes\":5169,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-14T20:38:50+00:00\",\"modified_at\":\"2026-09-14T20:38:52.432511+00:00\",\"file_provider\":\"native\",\"library_file_id\":\"libfile_214aa4e5e0688191afa618004aa535f8\",\"role\":\"editor\",\"result_index\":7,\"file_id\":\"file_00000000a81481fd9c676bfa500e4daf\",\"surface\":\"library\",\"score\":0.975232155220057,\"snippets\":[{\"text\":\"## Proposed physical end state\\n\\n**Stage 1 — whole-floor relocation (recommended):** move `Desktop\\\\GCE_DON` →\\n`C:\\\\Users\\\\Dekan AI Brother\\\\GCE_DON` (same internal layout, one cutover, one rollback), update the\\n7 dependency files + governance docs, Luce verifies, old location archived (not deleted).\\n\\n**Stage 2 — internal disposition (post-move, no time pressure):** archive `03_HANDOFFS` (after\\nsweeping its 2 unique files into the canonical bus), vestigial `00_INBOX`/`05_SIGNOFF_READY`/\\n`06_OUTBOX`, and `mailroom` (after its adjudication is closed). Route the loose CODA G1-G6 root\\nfile into the bus. Fix th