ile_provider\":\"native\",\"library_file_id\":\"libfile_697ff1d8ddf48191907a5f24d7667bde\",\"role\":\"editor\",\"result_index\":0,\"file_id\":\"file_00000000525c8246afa617bb83e7e24c\",\"surface\":\"library\",\"score\":0.9990966031226096,\"snippets\":[{\"text\":\"This is an operational exchange lane.\\r\\n\\r\\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\r\\n9. HANDOFF ENVELOPE\\r\\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\r\\n\\r\\nEvery transported handoff should use a structured envelope.\\r\\n\\r\\nWorking schema:\\r\\n\\r\\nHANDOFF_ID:\\r\\nFROM_SEAT:\\r\\nTO_SEAT:\\r\\nPROJECT:\\r\\nWORKSTREAM:\\r\\nTYPE:\\r\\nPRIORITY:\\r\\nSTATUS:\\r\\nCREATED_AT:\\r\\nRETURN_TO:\\r\\n\\r\\nOBJECTIVE:\\r\\n...\\r\\n\\r\\nCONTEXT:\\r\\n...\\r\\n\\r\\nINSTRUCTIONS:\\r\\n...\\r\\n\\r\\nARTIFACTS:\\r\\n...\\r\\n\\r\\nSTOP_CONDITIONS:\\r\\n...\\r\\n\\r\\nEXPECTED_RETURN:\\r\\n...\\r\\n\\r\\nExample:\\r\\n\\r\\nHANDOFF_ID: HDO-20260924-0017\\r\\nFROM_SEAT: Coda\\r\\nTO_SEAT: Luce\\r\\nPROJECT: GCE_DevPad_Command_Center\\r\\nWORKSTREAM: myDon Phase 1\\r\\nTYPE: VERIFICATION\\r\\nPRIORITY: NORMAL\\r\\nSTATUS: READY_TO_TRANSPORT\\r\\n\\r\\nOBJECTIVE:\\r\\nVerify route idempotency and restart persistence.\\r\\n\\r\\nCONTEXT:\\r\\n...\\r\\n\\r\\nRETURN_TO:\\r\\nCoda / Don\\r\\n\\r\\nThe filename should preserve the canonical handoff ID.\\r\\n\\r\\nExample:\\r\\n\\r\\nHDO-20260924-0017_luce_mydon_phase1.md\\r\\n\\r\\nor structured JSON where appropriate.\\r\\n\\r\\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\r\\n10. TWO-WAY REQUIREMENT\\r\\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\r\\n\\r\\nThe Cable Car cannot be outbound-only.\\r\\n\\r\\nCoda sends work into GCE.\\r\\n\\r\\nGCE must return:\\r\\n\\r\\n- findings;\\r\\n- implementation results;\\r\\n- verification;\\r\\n- blockers;\\r\\n- status;\\r\\n- artifacts;\\r\\n- escalation requests.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe same HANDOFF_ID should survive the full round trip.\\r\\n\\r\\nExample:\\r\\n\\r\\nHDO-20260924-0017\\r\\n    outbound Coda → Luce\\r\\n    return Luce → Coda\\r\\n\\r\\nDo not mint a disconnected identity for each leg unless there is a proven need.\\r\\n\\r\\nParent/child IDs may later be added for branching work.\\r\\n\\r\\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\r\\n11. GOOGLE DRIVE MCP ROLE\\r\\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\r\\n\\r\\nThe Drive integration should be evaluated for bounded operations such as:\\r\\n\\r\\n- create handoff artifact;\\r\\n- read handoff artifact;\\r\\n- move to a status folder;\\r\\n- archive completed work;\\r\\n- create return artifact;\\r\\n- inspect transport folder;\\r\\n- reconcile failed/incomplete delivery.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe design should avoid requiring Don to manually:\\r\\n\\r\\n- create files;\\r\\n- rename files;\\r\\n- move files;\\r\\n- copy payloads between folders;\\r\\n- clean up routine transport residue.\\r\\n\\r\\nAutomation should do routine transport housekeeping.\\r\\n\\r\\nDon should intervene only for:\\r\\n\\r\\n- routing authority;\\r\\n- conflict;\\r\\n- ambiguity;\\r\\n- escalation;\\r\\n- destructive cleanup if governance requires approval.\\r\\n\\r\\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\r\\n12. DRIVE CLEANUP / ARCHIVE POLICY\\r\\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\r\\n\\r\\nDon explicitly raised concern about Drive clutter.\\r\\n\\r\\nTherefore cleanup cannot be an afterthought.\\r\\n\\r\\nPotential lifecycle:\\r\\n\\r\\nREADY\\r\\n→ TRANSPORTED\\r\\n→ ACKNOWLEDGED\\r\\n→ COMPLETED\\r\\n→ ARCHIVED\\r\\n\\r\\nTransport artifacts should not remain forever in working folders.\\r\\n\\r\\nCandidate policy:\\r\\n\\r\\n- active/in-flight handoffs remain hot;\\r\\n- completed items move automatically to archive;\\r\\n- older operational transport residue can be compacted;\\r\\n- only artifacts with durable value get promoted into project/framework areas;\\r\\n- Raven/Magpie may later help classify durable records;\\r\\n- cleanup automation should never erase canonical project records.\\r\\n\\r\\nTransport archive != project canon.\\r\\n\\r\\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\r\\n13. RELATIONSHIP TO MAIN / ROOKIE DEVPAD\\r\\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\r\\n\\r\\nCable Car should eventually be able to target either operating surface.\\r\\n\\r\\nMain DevPad:\\r\\n\\r\\n- project-bound;\\r\\n- stable seats;\\r\\n- durable active work.\\r\\n\\r\\nRookie DevPad:\\r\\n\\r\\n- ad hoc;\\r\\n- experimental;\\r\\n- temporary runtime work.\"}],\"source_gizmo_id\":\"g-p-6ab41b7c2620819187c626358eeb8a48\",\"ref_id\":\"turn7file0\"},{\"version_id\":\"1\",\"name\":\"Pasted text(3).txt\",\"mime_type\":\"text/plain\",\"size_bytes\":53606,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-24T14:41:45+00:00\",\"modified_at\":\"2026-09-24T14:41:47.811482+00:00\",\"file_provider\":\"native\",\"library_file_id\":\"libfile_697ff1d8ddf48191907a5f24d7667bde\",\"role\":\"editor\",\"result_index\":1,\"file_id\":\"file_00000000525c8246afa617bb83e7e24c\",\"surface\":\"library\",\"score\":0.9981693683562302,\"snippets\":[{\"text\":\"──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\r\\n11. GOOGLE DRIVE MCP ROLE\\r\\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\r\\n\\r\\nThe Drive integration should be evaluated for bounded operations such as:\\r\\n\\r\\n- create handoff artifact;\\r\\n- read handoff artifact;\\r\\n- move to a status folder;\\r\\n- archive completed work;\\r\\n- create return artifact;\\r\\n- inspect transport folder;\\r\\n- reconcile failed/incomplete delivery.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe design should avoid requiring Don to manually:\\r\\n\\r\\n- create files;\\r\\n- rename files;\\r\\n- move files;\\r\\n- copy payloads between folders;\\r\\n- clean up routine transport residue.\\r\\n\\r\\nAutomation should do routine transport housekeeping.\\r\\n\\r\\nDon should intervene only for:\\r\\n\\r\\n- routing authority;\\r\\n- conflict;\\r\\n- ambiguity;\\r\\n- escalation;\\r\\n- destructive cleanup if governance requires approval.\\r\\n\\r\\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\r\\n12. DRIVE CLEANUP / ARCHIVE POLICY\\r\\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\r\\n\\r\\nDon explicitly raised concern about Drive clutter.\\r\\n\\r\\nTherefore cleanup cannot be an afterthought.\\r\\n\\r\\nPotential lifecycle:\\r\\n\\r\\nREADY\\r\\n→ TRANSPORTED\\r\\n→ ACKNOWLEDGED\\r\\n→ COMPLETED\\r\\n→ ARCHIVED\\r\\n\\r\\nTransport artifacts should not remain forever in working folders.\\r\\n\\r\\nCandidate policy:\\r\\n\\r\\n- active/in-flight handoffs remain hot;\\r\\n- completed items move automatically to archive;\\r\\n- older operational transport residue can be compacted;\\r\\n- only artifacts with durable value get promoted into project/framework areas;\\r\\n- Raven/Magpie may later help classify durable records;\\r\\n- cleanup automation should never erase canonical project records.\\r\\n\\r\\nTransport archive != project canon.\\r\\n\\r\\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\r\\n13. RELATIONSHIP TO MAIN / ROOKIE DEVPAD\\r\\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\r\\n\\r\\nCable Car should eventually be able to target either operating surface.\\r\\n\\r\\nMain DevPad:\\r\\n\\r\\n- project-bound;\\r\\n- stable seats;\\r\\n- durable active work.\\r\\n\\r\\nRookie DevPad:\\r\\n\\r\\n- ad hoc;\\r\\n- experimental;\\r\\n- temporary runtime work.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe transport envelope should identify project/workstream and desired seat, but\\r\\nmust not hard-code a DevPad surface unless required.\\r\\n\\r\\nmyDon may resolve the target surface based on current operating context.\\r\\n\\r\\nNo permanent assumption yet that:\\r\\n\\r\\none seat = one pad\\r\\none physical tile = one routing endpoint\\r\\n\\r\\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\r\\n14. RELATIONSHIP TO BEDROCK / OPENAI / KIMI / OTHER PROVIDERS\\r\\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\r\\n\\r\\nCompute providers remain separate.\\r\\n\\r\\nPotential Coda/runtime sources include:\\r\\n\\r\\n- ChatGPT;\\r\\n- OpenAI terminal/API if available;\\r\\n- Amazon Bedrock;\\r\\n- Kimi;\\r\\n- GLM;\\r\\n- other approved providers.\\r\\n\\r\\nBut:\\r\\n\\r\\nBEDROCK != TRANSPORT\\r\\nOPENAI != TRANSPORT\\r\\nKIMI != TRANSPORT\\r\\nOPENROUTER != TRANSPORT\\r\\nOPENCODE != TRANSPORT\\r\\n\\r\\nCable Car should remain model/provider-neutral.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe same handoff should be transportable regardless of which runtime occupies a\\r\\nseat.\\r\\n\\r\\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\r\\n15. FAILURE SEMANTICS\\r\\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\r\\n\\r\\nNo silent failure.\\r\\n\\r\\nCandidate hard failures:\\r\\n\\r\\n- Drive artifact missing;\\r\\n- duplicate canonical ID with conflicting payload;\\r\\n- malformed envelope;\\r\\n- unknown target seat;\\r\\n- local _shared write failure;\\r\\n- destination already exists with conflict;\\r\\n- return correlation failure;\\r\\n- archive move failure;\\r\\n- transport watcher unavailable.\\r\\n\\r\\nRequired behavior:\\r\\n\\r\\nFAIL VISIBLE\\r\\nDO NOT SILENTLY REROUTE\\r\\nDO NOT OVERWRITE CONFLICTING HANDOFF\\r\\nDO NOT INVENT TARGET\\r\\nDO NOT FALL BACK TO ANOTHER MODEL/SEAT\\r\\n\\r\\nSame-ID/same-payload duplicate may be treated as idempotent success after proof.\\r\\n\\r\\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\r\\n16.\"}],\"sourc