ve behavior exists in Cable Car methodology/design.  \n**NOT VERIFIED:** universal bootstrap enforcement across Coda/Nico/Luce/etc.  \n**GAP:** lifecycle ownership is not yet proven as a seat-level bootstrap invariant.  \n**RECOMMENDED TAXONOMY CHANGE:** make handoff lifecycle completion a universal bootstrap responsibility.\n\n════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════  \n**SESSION FOOTER**\n\n**CURRENT PHASE:** Framework taxonomy — handoff lifecycle  \n**CONFIDENCE:** **98%**\n\n**FINDING:**  \nAutomatic archive was designed for Cable Car, but I cannot verify it is universally baked into the active bootstrap.\n\n**NEW NON-NEGOTIABLE:**  \nAny seat/model that receives and ingests a handoff must complete its transport lifecycle and archive the completed handoff automatically.\n\n**EXCEPTION:**  \nDo not archive/remove canonical project or Framework records merely because their transport copy is complete.\n\n**NEXT ACTION:**  \nWhen we review the bootstrap taxonomy, explicitly locate and normalize the handoff lifecycle rule across all seats.\n\n**BUILD STATE:** NO BUILD AUTHORIZED  \n**CANON STATE:** REVIEW ONLY  \n**SESSION STATUS:** OPEN"]}, "create_time": 1790369944.975103, "end_turn": true, "id": "0e20c489-a88f-4910-b71d-d516299bd005", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations": [{"citation_format_type": "berry_file_search", "end_ix": 673, "metadata": {"extra": {"api_tool_source": "files/search", "authors_display": null, "cited_message_id": "92aea3e6-13f1-453a-b679-149cf063627b", "cited_message_idx": 198, "cloud_doc_url": "", "connector_id": null, "doi": null, "effective_time": null, "journal_homepage_url": null, "journal_name": null, "library_file_id": "libfile_697ff1d8ddf48191907a5f24d7667bde", "line_range": [1, 1], "publication_year": null, "retrieval_file_index": 0, "retrieval_turn": 7, "run_id": null, "search_result_idx": null, "set_id": null, "source_icon_url": null, "source_label": null, "source_url": null, "spl_version": null, "t