70026.869641, "end_turn": false, "id": "2d967883-96c6-42be-90c5-49058387186d", "metadata": {"can_save": false, "conversation_followup_suggestions_eligible": false, "cot_version": "v5", "default_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "finished_duration_sec": 8, "hide_inline_actions": true, "message_type": "next", "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "model_switcher_deny": [], "parent_id": "f90f0ffa-5290-4d0e-98b4-4e09013f8418", "reasoning_end_time": 1790370026.8327868, "reasoning_recap_type": "hide_all", "reasoning_start_time": 1790370018.1173236, "reasoning_status": "reasoning_ended", "request_id": "01041a41-d383-4ff2-8ee4-a53d4efd4fa4", "resolved_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "thinking_effort": "standard", "turn_exchange_id": "72a981be-6901-47af-abdd-e046615d8d35", "working_turn_id": "72a981be-6901-47af-abdd-e046615d8d35"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": 1790370026.869641, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {}, "name": null, "role": "assistant"}, "channel": "final", "content": {"content_type": "text", "parts": ["════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════  \n**GCE — LUCE NETWORK TRUTH TEST**  \n**SEAT:** Luce | **OCCUPANT:** Big Pickle  \n**MODE:** VERIFY / EVIDENCE ONLY  \n**CONFIDENCE:** **99%**  \n════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n\nYep. **One PowerShell block. One run.** No five-script bullshit.\n\nGive this whole thing to **Luce / actual Big Pickle** and have it run from the machine Space Bunny is using. It collects Wi-Fi state, gateway loss, Internet loss, DNS, latency/jitter, route evidence, and a `pathping` trace into one report.\n\n```powershell\n# ================================================================\n# GCE / LUCE — NETWORK + PACKET LOSS TRUTH TEST\n# MODE: READ-ONLY DIAGNOSTIC\n# PURPOSE: Determine whether Space Bunny instability is caused by\n#         local Wi-Fi, gateway loss, ISP/upstream loss, DNS, or WAN.\n# ================================================================\n\n$ErrorActionPreference = \"Continue\"\n$ts = Get-Date -Format \"yyyyMMdd_HHmmss\"\n$out = \"$env:USERPROFILE\\Desktop\\GCE_LUCE_NETWORK_TEST_$ts.txt\"\n\nfunction Log($s = \"\") {\n    $s | Tee-Object -FilePath $out -Append\n}\n\nfunction Ping-Test {\n    param(\n        [string]$Name,\n        [string]$Target,\n        [int]$Count = 100\n    )\n\n    Log \"\"\n    Log \"============================================================\"\n    Log \"PING TEST: $Name [$Target] — $Count packets\"\n    Log \"============================================================\"\n\n    $r = Test-Connection -TargetName $Target -Count $Count -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue\n\n    if (-not $r) {\n        Log \"RESULT: NO RESPONSES\"\n        return\n    }\n\n    $times = @($r | ForEach-Object { $_.Latency })\n    $received = $times.Count\n    $lost = $Count - $received\n    $lossPct = [math]::Round(($lost / $Count) * 100, 2)\n\n    $avg = [math]::Round(($times | Measure-Object -Average).Average, 2)\n    $min = ($times | Measure-Object -Minimum).Minimum\n    $max = ($times | Measure-Object -Maximum).Maximum\n\n    $jitterSamples = @()\n    for ($i = 1; $i -lt $times.Count; $i++) {\n        $jitterSamples += [math]::Abs($times[$i] - $times[$i-1])\n    }\n\n    $jitter = if ($jitterSamples.Count) {\n        [math]::Round(($jitterSamples | Measure-Object -Average).Average, 2)\n    } else { 0 }\n\n    Log \"Sent:       $Count\"\n    Log \"Received:   $received\"\n    Log \"Lost:       $lost\"\n    Log \"LOSS:       $lossPct %\"\n    Log \"Latency:    min=$min ms / avg=$avg ms / max=$max ms\"\n    Log \"Jitter avg: $jitter ms\"\n\n    if ($lossPct -gt 2) {\n        Log \"LUCE FLAG: SEVERE PACKET LOSS\"\n    }\n    elseif ($lossPct -gt 0) {\n        Log \"LUCE FLAG: PACKET LOSS PRESENT\"\n    }\n    elseif ($jitter -gt 30) {\n        Log \"LUCE FLAG: HIGH JITTER\"\n    }\n    else {\n        Log \"LUCE FLAG: CLEAN\"\n    }\n}\n\n\"============================================================\" | Set-Content $out\nLog \"GCE LUCE / BIG PICKLE — NETWORK TRUTH TEST\"\nLog \"Timestamp: $(Get-Date)\"\nLog \"Computer:  $env:COMPUTERNAME\"\nLog \"User:      $env:USERNAME\"\nLog \"============================================================\"\n\nLog \"\"\nLog \"### NETWORK ADAPTERS\"\nGet-NetAdapter |\n    Sort-Object Status,Name |\n    Format-Table Name,InterfaceDescription,Status,LinkSpeed -Auto |\n    Out-String | Log\n\nLog \"\"\nLog \"### WIFI RADIO / SIGNAL\"\n(netsh wlan show interfaces | Out-String) | Log\n\nLog \"\"\nLog \"### IP CONFIGURATION\"\n(ipconfig /all | Out-String) | Log\n\n# Determine active IPv4 default gateway\n$gw = (Get-NetRoute -DestinationPrefix \"0.0.0.0/0\" -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue |\n    Sort-Object RouteMetric |\n    Select-Object -First 1).NextHop\n\nLog \"\"\nLog \"ACTIVE DEFAULT GATEWAY: $gw\"\n\nif ($gw) {\n    Ping-Test \"LOCAL GATEWAY\" $gw 100\n}\n\nPing-Test \"CLOUDFLARE\" \"1.1.1.1\" 100\nPing-Test \"GOOGLE DNS\" \"8.8.8.8\" 100\nPing-Test \"DNS/HOSTNAME TEST\" \"cloudflare.com\" 100\n\nLog \"\"\nLog \"============================================================\"\nLog \"HTTPS CONNECTIVITY\"\nLog \"============================================================\"\n\nforeach ($hostName in @(\"1.1.1.1\",\"google.com\",\"github.com\")) {\n    Log \"\"\n    Log \"--- $hostName :443 ---\"\n    (Test-NetConnection $hostName -Port 443 -InformationLevel Detailed |\n        Format-List | Out-String) | Log\n}\n\nLog \"\"\nLog \"============================================================\"\nLog \"DNS TEST\"\nLog \"============================================================\"\n\nforeach ($name in @(\"google.com\",\"github.com\",\"openai.com\")) {\n    Log \"\"\n    Log \"--- $name ---\"\n    try {\n        (Resolve-DnsName $name -ErrorAction Stop |\n            Format-Table -Auto | Out-String) | Log\n    }\n    catch {\n        Log \"DNS FAILURE: $($_.Exception.Message)\"\n    }\n}\n\nLog \"\"\nLog \"============================================================\"\nLog \"ROUTE TRACE — 1.1.1.1\"\nLog \"============================================================\"\n(tracert -d 1.1.1.1 | Out-String) | Log\n\nLog \"\"\nLog \"============================================================\"\nLog \"PATHPING — 1.1.1.1\"\nLog \"THIS IS THE LONG TEST; LET IT FINISH.\"\nLog \"============================================================\"\n(pathping -n 1.1.1.1 | Out-String) | Log\n\nLog \"\"\nLog \"============================================================\"\nLog \"LUCE INTERPRETATION RULES\"\nLog \"============================================================\"\nLog \"1. Gateway loss > 0% = LOCAL WIFI / AP / HOTEL NETWORK problem.\"\nLog \"2. Gateway clean but 1.1.1.1 + 8.8.8.8 loss = ISP / hotel upstream problem.\"\nLog \"3. IP targets clean but hostname/DNS bad = DNS problem.\"\nLog \"4. 0% loss but large jitter/spikes = unstable/congested network.\"\nLog \"5. PATHPING should identify where persistent loss begins.\"\nLog \"6. Do NOT treat loss on one intermediate router alone as proof; routers may deprioritize ICMP.\"\nLog \"7. Final destination loss + application disconnects are the important correlation.\"\n\nLog \"\"\nLog \"============================================================\"\nLog \"REPORT COMPLETE\"\nLog \"Saved to:\"\nLog $out\nLog \"============================================================\"\n\nWrite-Host \"\"\nWrite-Host \"LUCE NETWORK TEST COMPLETE\"\nWrite-Host \"REPORT: $out\"\nWrite-Host \"\"\nnotepad $out\n```\n\n### What I want Luce to determine\n\n**Do not fix anything yet.** Luce should return only:\n\n> **LOCAL / HOTEL-WIFI / UPSTREAM-ISP / DNS / CLEAN-BUT-JITTERY / INCONCLUSIVE**  \n> Gateway packet loss: X%  \n> Internet packet loss: X%  \n> Average latency: X ms  \n> Jitter: X ms  \n> Worst hop: X  \n> **Does the evidence reasonably explain Space Bunny disconnecting/stalling? YES / NO / PARTIAL**\n\nIf that gateway test starts dropping packets, that's especially useful because it tells us the problem is happening **before we're even reaching the Internet**.\n\n════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════  \n**SESSION FOOTER**\n\n**CURRENT PHASE:** Temporary Space Bunny connectivity diagnosis  \n**CONFIDENCE:** **99%**  \n**RUNNING TAXONOMY CHECKLIST:** HELD — resume after network issue  \n**NEXT ACTION:** One Luce/Big Pickle network truth run; inspect one report.  \n**BUILD STATE:** NO BUILD AUTHORIZED  \n**SESSION STATUS:** OPEN"]}, "create_time": 1790370026.874577, "end_turn": true, "id": "5ca70be0-6ab9-43a2-a4af-8eb8e64a8928", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations": [], "code_blocks": {"0": {"edited": false, "id": "0q8i7u", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}}, "content_references": [], "conversation_followup_suggestions_eligible": true, "cot_version": "v5", "default_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "finish_details": {"stop_tokens": [200002], "type": "stop"}, "gizmo_id": "g-p-6ab43fca21d0819183966405a724bf5d", "is_complete": true, "message_type": "next", "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "model_switcher_deny": [], "notification_trigger_checkpoint": {"notification_id": "6ab6e10b2afc819192f0f672573c3597", "source": "responses", "source_id": null, "triggered_at": "2026-09-25T21:01:00.247768+00:00"}, "parent_id": "2d967883-96c6-42be-90c5-49058387186d", "request_id": "01041a41-d383-4ff2-8ee4-a53d4efd4fa4", "resolved_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "search_result_groups": [], "story_events": [], "thinking_effort": "standard", "turn_exchange_id": "72a981be-6901-47af-abdd-e046615d8d35", "working_turn_id": "72a981be-6901-47af-abdd-e046615d8d35"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": 1790370059.013895, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {}, "name": null, "role": "user"}, "channel": null, "content": {"content_type": "text", "parts": ["Okay, now your turn while I'm investigating this. Your turn is now to go through and reconcile our dis