g else:\n\n1. **Exact active Wi-Fi card**  \n2. **Exact current driver/version/provider/date for that card**  \n3. **What driver you previously updated/reset, and whether it was the same device**  \n4. **What software/filter layers sit between Windows and the network**\n\nIf the “driver update” was on a different adapter, then it tells us almost nothing about this current problem.\n\n**OWNER:** Luce  \n**CURRENT HYPOTHESIS:** client-side throughput limiter remains likely  \n**NEXT:** identify the exact active Intel card and its actual driver/software stack before any further reset  \n**CONFIDENCE:** 97% on the diagnostic direction"]}, "create_time": 1790373518.503325, "end_turn": true, "id": "3369cd59-ba5e-4987-a2fa-e0c3cd359be4", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations": [], "content_references": [], "conversation_followup_suggestions_eligible": true, "cot_version": "v5", "default_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "finish_details": {"stop_tokens": [200002], "type": "stop"}, "gizmo_id": "g-p-6ab43fca21d0819183966405a724bf5d", "is_complete": true, "message_type": "next", "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "model_switcher_deny": [], "parent_id": "ce22e029-253c-49db-bf6d-c2a73c7529d3", "request_id": "5bee3690-07dc-4f9b-ba00-c7e44f26ea63", "resolved_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "search_result_groups": [], "story_events": [], "thinking_effort": "standard", "turn_exchange_id": "03e2b521-9af0-49a2-b5bb-89fc1301033d", "working_turn_id": "03e2b521-9af0-49a2-b5bb-89fc1301033d"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": 1790373526.812823, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {}, "name": null, "role": "user"}, "channel": null, "content": {"content_type": "text", "parts": ["Perfect. We'll let him do it, and then let's go through this because this is ridiculous. I've never been on a Wi-Fi in a hotel that's 20 megabytes. Maybe my— again, we switch an IP. Maybe mine got fucking— whatever's on my computer from the MGM internet knows we're running a 