      Level3 403, SoftLayer/Panama errored. The ~19 Mbps ceiling is\n                      confirmed against Cloudflare's anycast edge ONLY. A cap specific\n                      to that edge path is not formally excluded.\n                   3. wlanreport + WFP filter dump REQUIRE ELEVATION - not attempted.\n                      Wi-Fi reason codes / driver-reset history unverified beyond the\n                      24h AutoConfig log (which was clean: 1 assoc, 0 disconnects).\n                   4. Single ~6 min window. Hotel load varies by hour; not sampled.\n                   5. Negotiated channel WIDTH is not exposed by netsh on this build.\n                      229 Mbps is consistent with 802.11ax 20 MHz 2SS, implying the AP\n                      may be serving 20 MHz - but that is NOT the throughput cause\n                      (229 PHY vs 19 goodput). Flagged, not concluded.\nNEXT ROUTE:        Don / Coda\nTWO THINGS THAT NEED YOUR ATTENTION\nThe stall monitor (PID 12068) is still running, but its samples from ~14:59–15:05 are invalid for stall correlation — the throughput tests saturated the link. Tell me whether to stop it or keep it armed.\nThis exonerates the network as the cause of the Space Bunny stalls for throughput — but note the irony: the earlier stall question and this one have different answers. The link is clean and fast-enough at the IP layer; the ~19 Mbps cap is a bandwidth limit, not a stability limit. It does not by itself explain disconnects.\n▣  Build · Big Pickle · 9m 16s"]}, "create_time": 1790376305.269, "end_turn": null, "id": "36ec0659-c47b-497d-b018-47f3bb25a4f2", "metadata": {"attachments": [{"height": 288, "id": "file_00000000a7f881f5961723fd0ac4ddd2", "library_file_id": "libfile_17217724bc7c8191aaeeaab8d8d0926d", "mime_type": "image/png", "name": "image(20260925-224444).png", "size": 17350, "width": 806}, {"height": 830, "id": "file_000000001de481f5ad1f7a55443a1872", "library_file_id": "libfile_7978f79dc01881919ae027a68ab47e8d"