entified an operating hypothesis:\n\nFor most ordinary GCE implementation work, the healthy default should be:\n\nDON ASK\n→ strategic framing\n→ methodology/architecture only where materially needed\n→ ONE COHERENT IMPLEMENTATION PASS\n→ internal testing during implementation\n→ RUNNABLE / VISIBLE ARTIFACT\n→ bounded verification\n→ bounded defect correction\n→ final verification\n→ CLOSE\n\nCore distinction:\n\nTESTING can happen during a build.\n\nDEBUGGING can happen during a build where necessary.\n\nBut the ORCHESTRATION FRAME should not continuously decompose and\nre-architect the work every time a minor test or verification finding appears.\n\nVerification is a control function, not automatically another design cycle.\n\nEvaluate whether the four sessions support, contradict, or qualify this\nhypothesis.\n\nDo NOT promote this hypothesis to permanent doctrine yet.\n\n────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nPHASE 5 — CONTROL-PLANE FINDINGS\n────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nThe postmortem must specifically examine three emerging controls.\n\n1. CODA ROLE BOUNDARY\n\nCoda remains strategic advisor / governance / framing / reconciliation.\n\nDetermine where Coda was allowed to become too operational or repeatedly\nreframe implementation from incomplete handoffs.\n\n2. SESSION CONTROLLER\n\nEvaluate the need for a distinct bounded runtime identity whose job is to:\n\n- instantiate the accepted Framework bootstrap,\n- establish the session header,\n- hold the current task boundary,\n- maintain the execution ledger,\n- preserve seat routing/state,\n- keep one coherent pass intact,\n- reject unnecessary branch creation,\n- enforce stop conditions,\n- produce the session footer.\n\nThis is an emerging role concept only.\nDo not name, canonize, or implement it during this recon.\n\n3. SENTINEL\n\nEvaluate separately the need for an OUTSIDE observer whose purpose is\nloop detection rather than session